  "query_preview": "..\nSW flow aloft will keep temperatures above normal through \nTuesday. A shortwave trough moves inland today and Tuesday from \nthe Pacific. This wave will move through Montana on Wednesday. The\nsystem will bring rain and snow Tuesday night and Wednesday with \na cold front. \n\nPrecipitation will begin as rain in the west late Tuesday night \nand spread east Wednesday morning. Temperatures will cool enough \nby Wednesday morning for either a rain/snow mix or change to all \nsnow in the west. Higher elevations of the Little Rocky Mountains\nnear Zortman has a potential for up to 3 inches of snow late\nTuesday night and Wednesday. Will issue a Winter Weather Advisory\nthere from 11 pm Tuesday night through 5 pm Wednesday afternoon. \n\nLocations along the Canadian Border west of Scobey could see up to\nan inch of snow. Snow amounts will depend on the timing of the \nrain to mixed precipitation and snow transitions. EC, GFS, and \nCMC ensembles continue to have varying higher snowfall amounts \nespecially NW of line from Zortman, Malta to Opheim so the snow \nforecast will need to watched in future model runs. As the main \nupper trough settles into the intermountain west Wednesday and \nThursday cooling aloft will drive temperatures closer to normal.\n\nLarge scale upper troughing continues across the western US the\nremainder of the the week. The next system will bring chances for\nlight snow Friday and Friday night. There is a fair amount of \nuncertainty in the quantity and spatial extent of precipitation, \nhowever, there is much higher confidence it will fall as snow \nrather than rain.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Lowered minimum temperatures Tuesday night and Wednesday. \n  Lowered high temperature Wednesday. \n\n- Raise QPF and snow amounts from NBM Tuesday night and Wednesday\n  to better match WPC Guidance.\n\n- Confidence in the pattern change on Tuesday night and Wednesday is\n  high.\n\n- Confidence in precipitation Tuesday night and Wednesday is high. \n\n- Confidence in Tuesday night and Wednesday snow forecast is low\n  overall with higher confidence that the Zortman area will\n  receive at least 2 inches of snow.",
